The '''God Wars Dungeon''' (often abbreviated as '''GWD'''), originally known as the '''Temple of Lost Ancients''',{{CiteNPC|npc=Ashuelot Reis|quote=Once Nex was no longer an immediate threat, they built the Temple of Lost Ancients around her. Most of the temple has since fallen to ruin, but you can still see some of the remains.}} is a [[dungeons|dungeon]] where armies of various [[gods]] fight, left over from the [[God Wars]].

The Dungeon was first released on [[28 August]] [[2007]], 18 days after the [[10 August]] 2007 [[August 2007 Archive of RuneScape|archive]] of RuneScape that ''Old School'' is based on. Its quick return to the live game was enabled by the fact that most of its assets had already been made at the time of the archive and it thus took minimal development time to recreate. One of the first major content releases following the February 2013 server launch, it passed [[Poll:Old School feature poll 9: God Wars & Banks|Old School Feature Poll #9]] on [[9 September]] [[2013]] with over 24,860 votes for the return, at an approval of 89%. GWD was then implemented on [[17 October]] for ''[[Old School RuneScape]]'' servers.

To get [[Slayer task|Slayer assignments]] related to the God Wars Dungeon, such as boss tasks, players must complete the [[Death Plateau]] quest.{{CiteTwitter|author=Mod Ash|url=https://twitter.com/JagexAsh/status/713027394320384000|date=24 March 2016|archiveurl=https://reldo.runescape.wiki/i/106915|archivedate=26 May 2020|quote=You do need Death Plateau for GWD tasks.}}
